# subloam-driver corrective cycle — three defects fixed, one honest end-test

The isolated sub-loam PTY driver had three verified defects. (1) The
submission path wrote the multi-KB frozen prompt in one write, slept a
fixed 0.5s, then sent the submit newline unconditionally — the real TUI
fragments a large write into multiple bracketed-paste segments and a
newline inside an open bracketed paste is literal text, so the turn was
never submitted. (2) The loop-ran / multi-turn classifier counted TUI
chrome alongside genuine markers, so a zero-model-action transcript
floated to multi-turn — the sealed AC.LIPW.4 real-binary green measured
nothing a TUI boot would not also satisfy. (3) No per-run cost/usage was
captured (the interactive driver emits no machine result envelope).

The fix is bounded and local: a paste-settle gate submits only after the
bracketed-paste echo goes quiet (delivery-path agnostic, any fragment
count); the loop signal is derived from genuine markers only with a
built-in falsification test; cost is real-or-honestly-absent via an
in-session /cost echo parse, never fabricated. The cycle ends at exactly
ONE honest re-test of the real frozen build_prompt — both terminal
outcomes (lives / dead-end) are equally valid and reported straight; the
cycle's value is the honest measurement of either polarity. The one
contaminated recorded result (the AC.LIPW.4 real-binary row) is
re-verified against its own written clause with an additive in-place
provenance note; no other recorded result is touched.

AC.SLF.{1,2,3,4,5,S} green against real test output. NOT merged to main,
NOT pushed, NOT published — sealed-local-on-branch is the deliverable.
